  "reason": "The best result so far is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. In the RNA-only multiprofile setting, transformer (0.653) and avgpool (0.650) aggregation were nearly identical, suggesting the aggregation choice may interact differently when combined with multimodal weighted fusion. Config_037 makes the single minimal change of swapping transformer for avgpool while retaining all other best-performing components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, weighted fusion). This isolates the aggregation effect in the multimodal weighted-fusion regime, where the interaction between profile aggregation and cross-modal fusion weights could shift the balance. As the final experiment, this is the highest-probability test to either marginally exceed 0.725 or confirm transformer as the optimal aggregation, while avoiding the low-probability alternatives (scgpt or PCA encoders, which were substantially weaker in RNA-only)."
}

